  "body": "Fixes #268.\n\n---\n\nAnother \"take care of old bugs\" fix.\n\nWhy not remove any mention of feed autodiscovery at all, you may ask, since only Firefox of the major browsers implements it?\n\nBecause this is one of those cases where we're catering to more user agents than just browsers! E.g. browser extensions that add feed autodiscovery to other browsers, or feed reader sites/apps that let you input urls like \"https://blog.whatwg.org/\" and they'll autodiscover the correct feed.\n",
